[2026-01-27 16:46:26,431: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Отправляем запрос на создание кандидата с данными: {'last_name': 'Anton', 'first_name': 'Dziavitsyn', 'externals': [{'auth_type': 'NATIVE', 'data': {'body': 'Anton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n1 \n\nI am a Software Engineer and Researcher \nwith 25+ years of practical experience in \nR&D and production projects worldwide. I \nparticipated and developed tens of projects \nin a wide range of areas: production \nautomation, BI systems, accounting systems, \nreporting systems, data processing systems, \nseismology, navigation, logistics, \ncartography, optics, engineering equipment, \nrobotics, sport analytics, and more... \nThousands of miles of code and tons of \nproject documentation were written by me. \n\nCompleted 80+ professional courses and \ncertifications. \n\nAuthor of educational programs in software \nengineering. \n\nActive scientific & technology researcher. \nInternational scientific research contributor. \nAuthor of 50+ scientific academic \npublications. \n\nAwards: \n\n2020, Senior Member, Association for \nComputing Machinery (ACM) \n\n2016, Trainer of the Year, Godel \nTechnologies Europe, Manchester High \nTech Park \n\n2020-2023, Several academic awards for \nactual scientific problems researching. \n\nExperience includes: \n\n• Scientific Research and IT R&D \n• Systems Analysis and Design \n• Technical Problem Solving, Team \n\nWorking \n• Software development  \n\nAnton Dziavitsyn \n\nAI/ML Research Engineer/Scientist \n\nLead Software Engineer / Computer \nScientist (R&D) \n\nPersonal Card \n\nBSU scientist profile (Russian) \n\nGoogle Scholar profile \n\nResearchGate profile \n\nLinkedIn profile \n\na.dziavitsyn@gmail.com \n\nTelegram: @adziavitsyn \n\nMinsk, Belarus \n\nhttps://www.dziavitsyn.name/\nhttps://mmf.bsu.by/ru/cathedras/web-technologies-and-computer-modeling/employees-wtcm/devitsyn-anton-sergeevich/\nhttps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=1Etu_toAAAAJ&hl=ru\nhttps://www.researchgate.net/profile/Anton-Dziavitsyn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/dziavitsyn/\nmailto:a.dziavitsyn@gmail.com\nhttps://t.me/adziavitsyn\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n2 \n\nSoftware Engineer and Researcher with 25+ years of practical experience in R&D and \nproduction projects worldwide. \n\nAuthor of Computer Science and Math publications and courses. Senior lecturer in \nMathematics faculty of Belarusian State University. \n\nProfessional certifications: \n\n ML Programmer to ML Architect \n\n Data Science Professional Certificate \n\n Advanced Data Science Specialist \n\n  Deep Learning  \n\n  .Net framework 4, Windows Applications \n\n Member of international scientific & professional organizations: \n\n• Association for Computing Machinery (ACM) – Senior Member \n• The European Mathematical Society (EMS) \n• European Association for Theoretical Computer Science (EATCS) \n\nBrief development technology/tools expertise chart \nProgramming languages: Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, C#, VB, Java, C++, Fortran \nTechnologies: Python/numpy/scipy/flask/django/ML libs and more… \n\nJavaScript/TypeScript/node.js/HTML/CSS/React/Angular/ and more… \n.NET ASP.NET/.NET core/Windows Forms/WCF/WPF/Silverlight \nHadoop/Apache Spark/SparkSQL/SparkML/ and more… \nContainers/Docker/Kubernetes/OpenShift/ and more… \nData Integration & processing/Hadoop/Drill/ and more… \n\nDatabases: MySQL, MS SQL, PostgreSql, OrientDB, MongoDB \nHTTP-servers: Apache, IIS, nginx \nIDE and tools: VSCode/JetBrains products/Visual Studio \nOperating systems: Windows, Linux, macOS \nProject tracking and bug \ntracking systems: \n\nMS Project, Rational Clear Quest, TFS, Jira, Confluence, Redmine \n\nSummary \n\nskillsoft™\n\n(©) deeplearning.ai\n\nhttps://skillsoft.digitalbadges.skillsoft.com/profile/antondziavitsyn674787/wallet\nhttps://www.youracclaim.com/badges/8aa5bc29-e240-4cf2-9c6b-867c8cd03c5f\nhttps://www.youracclaim.com/badges/762cfb97-8884-40aa-9914-e7ba01a4b778\nhttps://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/specialization/KUYW63EUWWK9\nhttps://www.acm.org/\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n3 \n\nResearch facility  \n\n2023 – 2024 \n\nLead AI/ML Research Engineer/Scientist \n\n• Developed concept & prototype of real-time distant gasometry system software. \nCreated real-time signal processing routines, indication on video in real-time \nwith using of Augmented Reality, data coding and processing methods. \n\n• Developed several AI-based prototypes for satellite image processing. (hyper-\nspectral images) \n\n• Developed methods for improving image quality and removing optical defects. \n\nAcronis - Schaffhausen Institute of Technology \n\n(Constructor group) \n\n2020 – 2023 \n\nLead AI/ML Research Engineer/Scientist \n• Developed concepts, methods, and prototypes, of parametric and Deep Learning-\n\nbased instruments for fluid dynamics process modeling. Subsequently, it was \nsuccessfully used in industry. \n\n• Developed concept and methods of real-time, indirect car tire degradation \nprediction for racing cars. \n\nAcronis – Toyota: https://youtu.be/xuxFn_zZMmc \n\n• Developed video analytic system concept and prototype for football matches. \nThe system combines game events and video records and displays video \nfragments based on analytical requests. Subsequently, it was successfully \nreleased and used in industry. \n\nAcronis – FC Ajax: https://youtu.be/tLhOYCe66PA \n\n• Developed methods for event data integration from different sources, methods of \ntime event corrections (when sources have wrong time or event data). \n\n• Developed prototypes for various analytic systems for real-time event analysis. \n\nWork experience \n(Details for last 10 years only) \n\nS2T\n\nhttps://www.acronis.com/\nhttps://institute.constructor.org/\nhttps://constructor.org/\nhttps://youtu.be/xuxFn_zZMmc\nhttps://youtu.be/tLhOYCe66PA\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n4 \n\n• Developed modules for AI based sport game tracking and event recognition \nsystems. \n\nAnton\'s expertise in machine learning and data analysis was truly impressive, and his contributions \nwere invaluable in helping us deliver a successful outcome. \nAnton\'s ideas and thoughtful approach helped us to develop truly exceptional solutions.  \nAnton is always willing to go the extra mile to ensure that the project was successful. \n\nSergey Ulasen, Senior Director of AI Development at Constructor group \n(Group of companies: Acronis, SIT, Rolos, Alemira, and others.) \n\nAnton\'s outstanding technical knowledge, innovative mindset, and strong work ethic have made him \nan invaluable asset to our team, particularly in the areas of Computational Fluid Dynamics surrogate \nmodeling and sports analytics. \nAnton possesses an exceptional aptitude for deep learning algorithms, and their ability to adapt and \nfine-tune these algorithms to various applications has been remarkable. In our CFD surrogate \nmodeling project, Anton developed a state-of-the-art model that dramatically reduced computational \ntime and cost, while maintaining the highest level of accuracy. This breakthrough allowed us to deliver \nour project within budget and ahead of schedule, garnering recognition and appreciation from our \nclients. \nThroughout our time working together, Anton has been a pleasure to collaborate with. He is a \ndedicated team player who consistently goes above and beyond to support his colleagues. Anton\'s \npositive attitude, strong communication skills, and willingness to share his knowledge have made him \nan invaluable member of our team. \nIn summary, I wholeheartedly recommend Anton for any position that requires deep learning \nexpertise, technical excellence, and a collaborative spirit. He is a talented and dedicated individual \nwho would be an asset to any organization. \n\nAndrey Adashchik, Team Lead – Acronis \n\nBelarusian State University \n\nwww.bsu.by \n\n2017 – Present \n\nSenior lecturer (Mathematics & Computer Science), Web-technologies and \ncomputer simulation department, Mechanics and Mathematics Faculty \n\n• Author and lecturer of the "Data analysis" course for MSc students \n• Author and lecturer of the "Python in production" course for MSc students \n• Author and lecturer of the "Android development" course \n• Author and lecturer of the "Linux systems family" course \n• Lecturer of various technology & CS courses \n\nhttps://www.bsu.by/\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n5 \n\nSelf-employed \n\n2019 – 2020 \n\nLead Software Engineer / Computer Scientist (R&D) \n\n• Organized and successfully implemented full software adaptation and migration \nof working company infrastructure (Azure -> AWS), with 130+ working \nservices, data storages, ML engines, rendering engines, etc. \n\n• Developed concept and methods of logistics optimization and control for \ncountry-wide cargo transportation company. \n\n• Successfully organized and led company web-services adaptation to meet EU \nweb security requirements. \n\ngalaktikasoft.com \n\n2018 – 2019 \n\nLead Software Engineer / Computer Scientist (R&D) \n\n• Developed concept and prototype of data integration solution to create, publish \nand manage data marts, and provide secure access to those by ODBC. \n\n• Developed OLAP compatible data presentation service using Open Source \ncomponents. \n\n• Developed several add-ons for PostgreSQL for cross db integration, custom data \ntype storage, data change logging and tracking. \n\nInvento Labs \n\ninvento-labs.com \n\n2017 – 2018 \n\nLead Software Engineer / Computer Scientist (R&D) \n\n• Developed methods and prototypes for video-based anthropometric \nmeasurements and analysis. Subsequently, it was successfully used in industry. \n\n• Developed data processing engine for data analytics using graph presentation, \nand a driver for orientDB. \n\n> Galaktikasoft\n\nf\n\ninventolabs:\n\nhttps://galaktikasoft.com/\nhttp://invento-labs.com/\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n6 \n\nGodel Technologies Europe \n\ngodeltech.com \n\n2015 – 2017 \n\nLead Software Engineer \n\n• Successfully led part of a software development project for improvement and \ntechnology upgrade of the booking system for a major global airline and tour \nprovider. \n\n• Developed data architecture and processing modules for a major goods logistics \nand storages provider. \n\nEPAM Systems \n\nepam.com \n\n2014 – 2015 \n\nSenior Software Engineer \n\n• Developed core modules for a new generation of contract management systems \nfor a major US insurance company. \n\nGodel Technologies Europe \n\ngodeltech.com \n\n2013 – 2014 \n\nSenior Software Engineer \n\n• Developed data processing modules for shop centers video analysis system. \n• Developed MS SQL server add-ons for binary data formats storage and \n\nprocessing (RBS) and caching providers. \n• Developed concept and prototype of web-based analytical dashboard and \n\ninstruments for a major investment company. \n\n1996 – 2014 Software Engineer in various companies... \n\n(cr) GODEL\nTECHNOLOGIES\n\nfo\n| <epam> |\n\nhttp://godeltech.com/\nhttp://www.epam.com/\nhttp://godeltech.com/\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n7 \n\nBelarussian State University \n\nbsu.by \n\n2016 – 2019 \n\nMathematics (Computer Science) \n\nPre-PhD (Mathematics, Computer Science expert) \n\nUniversity of Oxford \n\nox.ac.uk  \n\n2012 – 2014 \n\nMathematics and Computer Science \n\nAdvanced Diploma in Data and Systems Analysis \n\nBelarussian State University \n\nbsu.by \n\n2010 – 2016 \n\nMathematics (Computer Science) \n\nMSc (Mathematics, Computer Science expert) \n\nTechnical College \n\n1992 – 1995 \n\nAutomated control systems in production. Software developer. \n\nEducation \n\nUNIVERSITY OF\n\nOXFORD\n\nhttp://www.bsu.by/en/main.aspx\nhttp://www.ox.ac.uk/\nhttp://www.bsu.by/en/main.aspx\n\nAnton Dziavitsyn CV 2024 \n\n8 \n\n ML Programmer to ML Architect (70+ courses & exams) \n\n Data Science Professional Certificate (9 courses & exams) \n\n Advanced Data Science Specialist (4 courses & exams) \n\n  Deep Learning (5 courses & exams) \n\n  .Net framework 4, Windows Applications \n\n  Code School (10+ certificates in WEB development: JavaScript/Node.js/angular/Ember…) \n\n  20+ Mathematics & Computer Science courses \n\n• Association for Computing Machinery (ACM) – Senior Member \n• The European Mathematical Society (EMS) \n• European Association for Theoretical Computer Science (EATCS) \n\nACM Senior Member 2020 (Association for Computing Machinery) \n\nTrainer of the Year 2016 (Godel Technologies Europe, Manchester High Tech Park) \n\nWas awarded for the creation of educational lectures and training courses for \nengineers... \n\n• Author and lecturer of the software development course lectures \n\n• Open-Source contributor (GitHub, PyPi, Apache projects, Docker Hub, Red Hat \ncommunity, Debian community…) \n\n• Software Developers community member (Microsoft, IBM, Google, RedHat, \nWolfram Research…) \n\nCertifications and courses \n\nMembership in international organizations \n\nAwards \n\nOther professional activities \n\ncoursera\n\nhttps://skillsoft.digitalbadges.skillsoft.com/profile/antondziavitsyn674787/wallet\nhttps://www.youracclaim.com/badges/8aa5bc29-e240-4cf2-9c6b-867c8cd03c5f\nhttps://www.youracclaim.com/badges/762cfb97-8884-40aa-9914-e7ba01a4b778\nhttps://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/specialization/KUYW63EUWWK9\nhttps://www.acm.org/\nhttps://www.youtube.com/c/AntonDziavitsyn'}}], 'middle_name': 'оформлен', 'email': 'a.dziavitsyn@gmail.com', 'social': [{'social_type': 'TELEGRAM', 'value': '@adziavitsyn'}], 'photo': 104975519, 'files': [104975512]}
