ing Corps (October 2018 – September 2021)\n\nMath/Reading  Corps is a data-driven tutoring program, and it uses assessment data to identify\n\nРезюме обновлено 18 ноября 2022 в 11:53 \n\nGJ rabota.by\n\nat-risk students, target instruction and monitor student progress during intervention.\n    • Requirements analysis and testing\n    • Test estimation\n    • Test environment preparation\n    • Creating and executing Test Cases\n    • Bug reporting\n    • Carrying out functional, regression, cross-browsers, mobile testing\n    • Carrying out database testing\n    • Working with developer's team to reproduce the issues and resolve problems\n\nTools and environment: Jira, Confluence, Zephyr for Jira, BrowserStack, MySQL Workbench, Bamboo\n\nTraining: Web Apps Services Testing (February-March 2019)\nListener\n\nThe training program covered the following aspects required for testing REST and SOAP web\nservices:\n    • Client-server architecture of web applications\n    • Protocols (TCP/IP, HTTP(S), SSH)\n    • Utilities (Putty, Fiddler, Postman, SOAP UI),\n    • Languages (XML, JSON, HTML)\n    • Web testing methods and types of authentication\n    • Performed API testing\n    • Automated test suites in Postman\n    • Automated testing scenarios in SOAP UI\n\nEnvironment: Windows 10, Android 5\nTools and Technologies: Putty, Fiddler, Postman, SOAP UI\n\nTraining: Mobile Testing (May-June 2020)\nListener\nThe training program covered the following aspects:\n    • Mobile Testing Strategy and Challenges\n    • Types of Mobile Applications\n    • Pros and Cons of mobile testing on Real Devices, Simulators and Emulators\n    • Utilities for mobile testing (Android Studio, Charles Proxy, ADB)\n    • Performed network testing with weak/normal connection\n    • Performed accessibility testing for mobile app (Talk Back on Android)\nEnvironment: Windows 10, Android 10\nTools and Technologies: Android Studio, Fiddler, Charles Proxy, Talk Back\n\nОктябрь 2015\xa0—\nОктябрь 2018\n3 г