[2026-01-27 17:17:46,674: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104979936, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/4/2/1/4218dabfdab2812d97930d14c8f32583.pdf/Chahan%2520Aliaksei.pdf?s=ALksD2a6iDoFKN-InrODlg&e=1769566666', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'Chahan%20Aliaksei.pdf', 'text': "Chahan Aliaksei\nMale, 38\xa0years, born on 29 July 1984\n\nThe phone has been hidden by the job seeker\nachahan@gmail.com\xa0—\xa0preferred means of communication\n\nReside in: Minsk\nCitizenship: Belarus,\xa0work permit at: Belarus\nNot ready to relocate, ready for business trips\n\nDesired position and salary\n\nLead Test Automation Engineer\nSpecializations:\n\n—  Programmer, developer\n—  Tester\n\nEmployment: part time, full time\nWork schedule: remote working, flexible schedule, full day, shift schedule\nDesired travel time to work: any\n\nWork experience — 17 years 2 months\nMay 2020\xa0— till\nnow\n2 years 7 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nMinsk,\xa0www.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nLead Software Test Automation Engineer\nTest Automation\n\nApril 2020\xa0— May\n2020\n2 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nMinsk,\xa0www.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nLead automation engineer\nBeeing a part of the team implementing POC for one of commercial banks was responsible for:\n- Close communication with management and dev. teams (mostly backend).\n- Implementing backend testing solution.\n- Testing backend API.\n- Implementing POC for native mobile app. testing solution.\n- Implementing POC for Web UI testing solution with mobile devices support.\n\nAll solutions implemented for automated testing were presented for a customer as part of final demo.\n\nOctober 2019\xa0—\nJanuary 2020\n4 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nMinsk,\xa0www.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nLead Software Test Automation Engineer\nAs a testing team lead was involved in new project discovery phase, onsite in customers office.\nGather necessary information on test automation perspectives for the customer.\nPropose/introduce automation solution for customer.\n\nResume updated 14 November 2022 at 17:38\n\nGJ rabota.by\n\nCustomer:\nis a British financial services comparison website. It provides comparison details for financial products\nincluding car insurance, home and pet insurance, home heating payments and breakdown cover.\n\nMarch 2018\xa0—\nOctober 2019\n1 year 8 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nMinsk,\xa0www.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nLead software test automation engineer\nParticipation:\nAs an automation lead was responsible for the following activities:\n- build Web UI (desktop and mobile support) and back-end testing frameworks from scratch\n- set up automation process for several scrum teams on a project\n- build and maintain test execution infrastructure from scratch. Implemented solution was used as a\npart of CI/CD process.\n- implement set of regression tests: integration, mobile web, desktop web.\nAs an automation consultant for several projects:\n- implemented solution, which then was used across several scrum teams (visual UI testing).\n- proposed and introduced improvements to existing test framework implemented by one of scrum\nteams in order to support mobile Web testing on real devices and in mobile cloud\n\nTools and Technologies:\nSelenium WebDriver, Appium, TestNg, Gradle, Docker, docker-selenium, Jenkins, Google Guice,\nGoogle Gson, Browserstack, Retrofit 2, Git, Java 8, HTTP, JSON, RESTful Web Services, Web UI\n\nCustomer:\nis a French multinational corporation specializing in electrical equipment that is headquartered in\nRueil-Malmaison, France.\n\nMay 2015\xa0—\nNovember 2018\n3 years 7 months\n\nN/a\nMinsk\n\nLead software engineer in test\nAs a remote member of distributed across several countries (time zones) team consisting of 7\nengineers was involved RESTful web services automated testing:\n  - web services integration testing\n  - back-end business logic validation\n  - daily communication with remote team and customer management\n  - existing API testing framework, automation processes and standards improvement\n  - mentoring automation engineer who worked remotely\n\nTools and Technologies:\nJava 8, Apache Http Client, Google Gson, Maven, TestNg, iBatis, Oracle DB\n\nCustomer:\nis an American peer-to-peer lending company, headquartered in San Francisco, California. It was the\nfirst peer-to-peer lender to register its offerings as securities with the Securities and Exchange\nCommission (SEC), and to offer loan trading on a secondary market. The company is the world's\nlargest peer-to-peer lending platform.\n\nSeptember 2016\n— March 2018\n1 year 7 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nMinsk,\xa0www.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nChahan Aliaksei  •  Resume updated 14 November 2022 at 17:38\n\nLead software test automation engineer\nParticipation:\nAs a lead automation engineer was involved in the following activities:\n- mentoring and supporting remote automation team in their daily activities\n- involved in setting up and improvement of automation process, best practices and coding standards\nfor multiple scrum teams including remote ones\n- implement set of testing tools used by different scrum teams in their automation efforts. e.g. a tool\nwhich allowed to persist test data between automation runs in JanRain system.\n- Web UI test automation framework creation and setup\n- desktop/mobile automated tests implementatio