[2026-01-27 17:18:09,524: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104980019, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/c/9/e/c9ef96ac83783413d0360a95aae1c4f4.pdf/CV%2520-%2520Kirill%2520Kaluga%2520-%2520Lead%2520SET.pdf?s=wVI8NO4uGgcQd-JAshpojA&e=1769566689', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'CV%20-%20Kirill%20Kaluga%20-%20Lead%20SET.pdf', 'text': 'KIRILL KALUGA \nSenior/Lead Software Engineer in Test \n\nMinsk, Belarus · +375296171033 \nkirill.kaluga.s@gmail.com · LinkedIn Profile \n\nSKILLS \n• 2+ years of Team Supervising, Leading experience \n\n• 1+ year of delivery management backup person \nand Head of AQA department (5 ppl) experience \n\n• ability to adapt easily to new environments and \nreact quickly to new challenges \n\n• good team player skills willing to reach a consensus \non contentious issues \n\n• with possibility to construct business relationships \nwith English-speaking customer via any type of \ncommunication \n\n• spend free time in mentoring and educational \nactivities  \n\n• advanced experience in UI Automation \ntesting and experience with Web \nServices Testing \n\n• Languages: Java, Groovy \n\n• Java Tools & Frameworks: Frameworks \n(Junit4, TestNG), Auto Tools (Selenium, \nREST-assured), Testing Tools (AssertJ, \nJoda-Time, Apache POI) \n\n• Infrastructure tools: VM (IBM VM), \nCloud (EPAM Cloud, AWS, Azure), \nContainerization (Docker), CI (Jenkins, \nAzure DevOps) etc. \n\nEXPERIENCE \n\nAPR 2022 – TILL NOW \n\nSENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER IN TEST, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: NDA, American multinational mass media and entertainment conglomerate \nProject Role: Key Software Engineer in Test \nTasks performed: This project is more about coding and testing. The main purpose of the project \nis migration from old generation of account management system to actual technology stack. So, I \nmost was involved in the following activities:  \n\n• test cases automation both for old & new applications, exploratory testing \n\n• enhancements into existing automation framework \n\n• support migration and release activities \n\n• mentoring of junior members of the team \n\nAPR 2021 – MAR 2022 \n\nSENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER IN TEST, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: NDA, one of the top 5 investment banks \nProject Role: Test Team Lead / Demand Owner for Account \nTasks performed: Here I played the role of SWAT Team Lead, which means that my team takes \nmanual backlog, automates it and transfers it to regression team. It included next actions: \n1. Present the team: \n\n• presenting team during management sync up \n\n• communication with management, stakeholders and backlog-owners/responsible persons \n\n• analysis of incoming backlogs, providing high-level estimations / assisting with detailed \n2. Lead the team:  \n\n• coordination of team assignments, keeping ongoing track \n\n• code review in "officer" role, being mediator in discussions and expert in case of tricky issues \n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/kirill-kaluga-32b314a3/\n\n2 \n\n• monthly-based retrospective sessions with sharing results to management \n\n• building relationships inside the team \n3. Grow the team:  \n\n• staffing and interviewing for SWAT team and whole QA project  \n\n• organization and delegation of mentoring and support for newly joined teammates \n\n• endorsing teammates to be proactive, think outside the box and make improvements \n\n• providing delivery/health reports for DM/RM  \n\n• developing of teammates with some ideas/requests to their PDPs, assisting them with \ngetting new titles (both E2->E3 and E1->E2) \n\nFEB 2021 – MAR 2022 \n\nSENIOR/LEAD SOFTWARE ENGINEER IN TEST, EXPERT SOFT \nCustomer: NDA, one of "the Big Three" rating agencies \nProject Role: Key Tester for Customer / Head of Automation QA for Company \nTasks performed: During the assignment for the customer, it was work as Key Quality Engineer \ninside of Scrum Dev Team and I participated in the following activities: \n\n• test cases writing and manual testing of newly introduced functionalities \n\n• making decisions “to automate” and implementing new test automation scenarios \n\n• introducing enhancements in TAF, code review activities \n\n• participation in releases and regression activities \n\n• initiation and participation in investigation of environments and 3rd-party instabilities \nAs Head of AQA next items were related to me: \n\n• present the company during the pre-sales \n\n• grow and developing of the teammates, including compensation review \n\n• preparation of the teammates for customer’s interview \n\n• staffing and interviewing candidates for the company \n\nOCT 2020 – FEB 2021 \n\nSENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER IN TEST, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: NDA \nProject Role: Key Tester \nTasks performed: During this period there were several short-term assignments, with the \nfollowing activities: \n\n• assisting and orchestrating of test automation migration from proprietary customer’s tools to \nopen-source solutions such as Jenkins, ReportPortal etc. \n\n• enhancements in TAF, implementing new test automation scenarios  \n\n• participation in Resource development programs and activities, such as Test Automation Lab \n\n• more involvement into university educational activities \n\nFEB 2020 – OCT 2020 \n\nSENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER IN TEST, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: Burberry, Retail & Distribution \nProject Role: Key Tester, Test Stream Lead \nTasks performed: During my work on Payment & Fulfillment Test Automation Stream I\'d been \nparticipating in the following activities: \n\n• representing for customer and leading P&F Test Automation stream (4 engineers) \n\n• enhancements in TAF, implementing new test automation scenarios  \n\n• participation in releases as TA Release Lead over all BURB-ATG TA streams \n\n• initiation and participation in investigation of environments and 3rd-party instabilities \n\n• being involved in rework of Testing and Release strategies \n\n3 \n\n• mentoring of manual QA engineers in TA discipline on the project \n\nFEB 2018 – DEC 2019 \n\nSOFTWARE TEST AUTOMATION ENGINEER, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: Business Information and Media, Thomson Reuters \nProject Role: 1st stage: Tester, Test Infrastructure Supporter \n 2nd stage: Mentor, Team Supervisor, Acting Test Architect  \nTasks performed: During the first stage, there was key tester role in Regression team: \n\n• providing visibility of the ongoing health and stability of application based on regression  \n\n• building communication with customer-side colleagues, business/product-owners \n\n• active participation in design of new clean code process and performing refactoring \n\n• leading of test suites reworking process, including developing of approaches and best \npractices, creation and support of appropriate technical documentation \n\n• optimizing test infrastructure state in cooperation with Test Architect \nOn the second stage I proceed with: \n\n• being as regression test team member and assistant for Test architect in various tasks, such \nas migration from dedicated VM to Customer’s AWS solution \n\n• being proactive and prevention of product issues due to Infrastructure Exit Program \nHowever, I mostly participated in migration to EPAM India. This action includes: \n\n• preparation and implementation of KT plan, online and live trainings, KT and QA sessions \nespecially during BT \n\n• technical and soft skills mentoring of new team in EPAM India \n\n• presenting of Minsk Regression Team in India and building relationships between teams  \n\n• detecting and resolving team coordination issues, completing final steps of “soft launch”  \n\nNOV 2016 – JAN 2018  \n\nJUNIOR/MIDDLE SOFTWARE TEST AUTOMATION ENGINEER, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: Human Recognition, EPAM Systems \nProject Role: Key Tester, Scrum Master \nTasks performed: Development and delivery of human recognition product based on rapidly \nchanging requirements and following EPAM internal application architecture strategy. My \npersonal responsibilities and tasks were: \n\n• resolving of existing test automation bugs, increasing UI tests coverage \n\n• improving of test analysis process work and constructing integration with ReportPortal \n\n• migration to new CI based on EPAM Cloud with decreasing of test suites execution time \n\n• optimization of test strategy and increasing role of Automation testing in regression testing \n\n• performing scrum-mastering activities and moving team to Scrumban process \n\nAUG-2016 - NOV-2016  \n\nJUNIOR SOFTWARE TEST AUTOMATION ENGINEER, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: Travel & Hospitality, IHG \nProject Role: Key Tester, Test Stream Lead \nTasks performed: During my work on IHG API stream there were following activities: \n\n• implementation of new tests (REST, SOAP and UI) based on user stories \n\n• resolving of existing test automation bugs and refactoring of test framework \n\n4 \n\nEDUCATIONAL ACTIVTIES \n\nAUG 2018 – FEB 2022 \n\nASSITANT LECTURER, BELARUSIAN STATE TECHNOLOGICAL UNIVERSITY \nActivities performed: Gained some experience during EPAM TAT Lab program and BSU lecturing, \nI accepted the proposal of BSTU to conduct the “Software Testing” course. So, there was almost \nthe same process as for BSU, however, the result of this course was exams, so I: \n\n• analyzed educational program and background of students \n\n• adopted existing tasks \n\n• added additional tasks, based on specific background of students \n\nAUG 2017 – FEB 2022 \n\nASSITANT LECTURER, BELARUSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nActivities performed: Here I was involved in university lecturing program. That is partnership \nbetween EPAM and Belarusian universities. So, I started from BSU, as assistant for Vitali Shulha. \nNext years, all the responsibilities were fully transferred from Vitali to me. They include: \n\n• adopting TA educational program up to preparation level of the students \n\n• providing lecturing and Q&A support for easy-going usage of TA Lab educational program \n\n• task performance review, providing feedback to the students \n\n• conducting examinations and re-examinations (if needed) in the end of the course \n\nJUL 2018 – FEB 2021 \n\nLAB MENTOR, EPAM SYSTEMS, TEST AUTOMATION LAB BELARUS & CIS \nActivities performed: After gaining experience with TA Lab and university, I assisted Vitali Shulha \nin starting completely new Test Automation Lab educational program: \n\n• reviewing and providing feedback for several iterations of online course and offline lab \n\n• participating in processes developing, playing role “mentor zero” \n\n• testing, providing feedback, implement improvements in started process \n\n• review and assisting students on the different stages of this new process \n\n• onboarding and assisting new mentors \n\nMAR 2017 – FEB 2019 \n\nTEAM MENTOR, EPAM SYSTEMS, TEST AUTOMATION LAB BELARUS \nActivities performed: I started my educational career as Team Mentor in old version of Test \nAutomation Lab of EPAM Belarus. During this time, my main responsibilities were about: \n\n• coordination of team assignments, keeping ongoing track \n\n• introduction into agile ceremonies and workflows of test automation and QA teams \n\n• conducting code reviews and performing “debriefing” and retrospective sessions \n\n• making “demo sessions” for Lab Head, providing team and individual reports for Lab Head \n\nEDUCATION \nJUNE 2020 \n\nMASTER’S DEGREE, BELARUSSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nFaculty: Mechanics and Mathematics  \nDegree (diploma): Master in “Math and computer science” \n\nJUNE 2017 \n\nSPECIALIST’S DEGREE, BELARUSSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nFaculty: Mechanics and Mathematics \nSpecialty: Mathematic, IT specialist (Mobile  development) \n\n\tExperience\n\tEDUCATIONAL ACTIVTIES\n\tEDUCATION', 'fields': {'name': None, 'birthdate': None, 'phones': ['+375296171033'], 'email': 'kirill.kaluga.s@gmail.com', 'salary': None, 'position': None, 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': None}, 'parsing_meta': {'last_names_ignored': False, 'emails_ignored': False, 'phones_ignored': False}}
