ration with ReportPortal \n\n• migration to new CI based on EPAM Cloud with decreasing of test suites execution time \n\n• optimization of test strategy and increasing role of Automation testing in regression testing \n\n• performing scrum-mastering activities and moving team to Scrumban process \n\nAUG-2016 - NOV-2016  \n\nJUNIOR SOFTWARE TEST AUTOMATION ENGINEER, EPAM SYSTEMS \nCustomer: Travel & Hospitality, IHG \nProject Role: Key Tester, Test Stream Lead \nTasks performed: During my work on IHG API stream there were following activities: \n\n• implementation of new tests (REST, SOAP and UI) based on user stories \n\n• resolving of existing test automation bugs and refactoring of test framework \n\n4 \n\nEDUCATIONAL ACTIVTIES \n\nAUG 2018 – FEB 2022 \n\nASSITANT LECTURER, BELARUSIAN STATE TECHNOLOGICAL UNIVERSITY \nActivities performed: Gained some experience during EPAM TAT Lab program and BSU lecturing, \nI accepted the proposal of BSTU to conduct the “Software Testing” course. So, there was almost \nthe same process as for BSU, however, the result of this course was exams, so I: \n\n• analyzed educational program and background of students \n\n• adopted existing tasks \n\n• added additional tasks, based on specific background of students \n\nAUG 2017 – FEB 2022 \n\nASSITANT LECTURER, BELARUSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nActivities performed: Here I was involved in university lecturing program. That is partnership \nbetween EPAM and Belarusian universities. So, I started from BSU, as assistant for Vitali Shulha. \nNext years, all the responsibilities were fully transferred from Vitali to me. They include: \n\n• adopting TA educational program up to preparation level of the students \n\n• providing lecturing and Q&A support for easy-going usage of TA Lab educational program \n\n• task performance review, providing feedback to the students \n\n• conducting examinations and re-examinations (if needed) in the end of the course \n\nJUL 2018 – FEB 2021 \n\nLAB MENTOR, EPAM SYSTEMS, TEST AUTOMATION LAB BELARUS & CIS \nActivities performed: After gaining experience with TA Lab and university, I assisted Vitali Shulha \nin starting completely new Test Automation Lab educational program: \n\n• reviewing and providing feedback for several iterations of online course and offline lab \n\n• participating in processes developing, playing role “mentor zero” \n\n• testing, providing feedback, implement improvements in started process \n\n• review and assisting students on the different stages of this new process \n\n• onboarding and assisting new mentors \n\nMAR 2017 – FEB 2019 \n\nTEAM MENTOR, EPAM SYSTEMS, TEST AUTOMATION LAB BELARUS \nActivities performed: I started my educational career as Team Mentor in old version of Test \nAutomation Lab of EPAM Belarus. During this time, my main responsibilities were about: \n\n• coordination of team assignments, keeping ongoing track \n\n• introduction into agile ceremonies and workflows of test automation and QA teams \n\n• conducting code reviews and performing “debriefing” and retrospective sessions \n\n• making “demo sessions” for Lab Head, providing team and individual reports for Lab Head \n\nEDUCATION \nJUNE 2020 \n\nMASTER’S DEGREE, BELARUSSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nFaculty: Mechanics and Mathematics  \nDegree (diploma): Master in “Math and computer science” \n\nJUNE 2017 \n\nSPECIALIST’S DEGREE, BELARUSSIAN STATE UNIVERSITY \nFaculty: Mechanics and Mathematics \nSpecialty: Mathematic, IT specialist (Mobile  development) \n\n\tExperience\n\tEDUCATIONAL ACTIVTIES\n\tEDUCATION'}}]}
