lemented items, so both developers and new TA Engineers can\neasily use these tools\n• Performed multiple Knowledge Transfer sessions to solve all found questions, blockers and shared\nthe way how people can investigate TA issues without me\n\nFebruary 2016\xa0—\ntill now\n6 years 10 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nwww.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nNon-project Activities\n• Performed more than 50 Technical Interviews for people from market all over the world from Junior\nto Lead Level and defined if person fits the level he/she applies from technical side\n• Performed more than 30 Project Interviews for people inside EPAM to define if person fits specific\nproject/position (about 30% of such interviews as a not associated with a project Technical Interviewer)\n• Performed as a Resource Manager for 2 subordinates (conflict-solving,  discussing related news\n\nResume updated 20 November 2022 at 22:15\n\nGJ rabota.by\n\nacross Company, helping with project search, helping with Personal Development Plan and Level Up,\nmanaging salaries)\n• Mentored more than 10 specialists in Test Automation Mentoring program (2 from Trainee/Not TA\nSpecialist to Junior, 4 from Junior to Middle, 5 from Middle to Senior level)\n• Volunteered at EPAM UpSkill Lab Project created to help non-IT specialists reinvest their careers\n(Mentored 4 persons from zero to Trainee/Junior level)\n•  Participated as a part of Assessment committee to define if candidate is ready to raise his level\n(Middle to Senior, Senior to Lead)\n\nMarch 2021\xa0—\nApril 2022\n1 year 2 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nwww.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nSenior Test Automation Engineer\n• Performed as a Tech Lead for a team of 4 to 10 Test Automation Engineers\n• Mentored Junior and Middle level specialists to improve their skills and help to level up (during\nproject and 2 months period after it, 3 team members changed their title: 2 Junior -> Middle, 1 Middle\n-> Senior)\n• Onboarded newcomers\n• Created Test Automation Framework base structure before other team members start writing tests\nusing it, to ensure everything will be consistent and similar code-style will be applied by all the\nteammates\n• Performed Code Review for all tasks and changes done by the team\n• Held multiple Knowledge Transfer sessions to share my experience with the team: about tools,\ncode-style, patterns and anti-patterns, mentoring, etc.\n\nNovember 2017\n— March 2021\n3 years 5 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nwww.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nTest Automation Engineer\nCreated Test Automation Framework under supervision\n\nAugust 2016\xa0—\nNovember 2017\n1 year 4 months\n\nEPAM Systems Inc (Беларусь)\nwww.epam.by\nIT, System Integration, Internet\n\n• System Integration, Technological and Business Processes Automation, IT Consulting\n\nJunior Test Automation Engineer\nAutomated test cases under supervision\n\nJuly 2014\xa0— July\n2016\n2 years 1 month\n\nWargaming.net\nFunctional Testing Engineer\nTested new maps, vehicles and balance\n\nEducation\n\nMaster\n\n2019 Belarusian State University of Informatics and Radioelectronics, Minsk\nComputer systems and networks, Mathematics. Computer Sciences\n\n2017 Belarusian State University, Minsk\n\nZaitsev Evgeny  •  Resume updated 20 November 2022 at 22:15\n\nApplied Mathematics and Informatics, Applied Mathematics and Informatics\n\nKey skills\nLanguages Russian — Native\n\nEnglish — B1 — Intermediate\n\nSkills  Leadership Skills      Customer orientation      Communication skills      Mentoring \n\n Interviews      Analytical skills      Английский язык      Negotiation skills \n\n Presentation skills      Teamleading \n\nFurther 