[2026-01-27 17:18:56,787: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Базовые данные кандидата: {'last_name': 'Pavel', 'first_name': 'Stryhelski', 'externals': [{'auth_type': 'NATIVE', 'data': {'body': 'Contact\n\nwww.linkedin.com/in/pavel-\nstryhelski-462748bb (LinkedIn)\n\nTop Skills\nC#\nJava\nSelenium\n\nLanguages\nEnglish (Professional Working)\n\nCertifications\nComplete Guide to Test Automation:\nTechniques, Practices, and Patterns\nfor Building and Maintaining Effective\nSoftware Projects\nTeamLead:101 course\nEffective 1-to-1\nSelenium WebDriver with Docker\n\nPavel Stryhelski\nTest Automation Manager at Aras Corporation\nMinsk, Belarus\n\nSummary\nI`m a Test automation manager with 9+ years of experience in\nQA and Test automation. I really like working with people, building\na team, interviewing and hiring new people, see how they grow\nand help them to do it. Another part is to be involved into business\nprocesses: to understand how automation itself and improving\nprocesses can help a company to grow, to reduce cost of manual\nwork, be flexible, release/fail/recover fast. I like cross department\ncommunication to be on the same page with QAs, developers,\ndevops and managers to achieve goals.\n\nExperience\n\nAras Corporation\n1 year 7 months\n\nSDET team`s Product Owner\nNovember 2021\xa0-\xa0Present\xa0(1 year 2 months)\n\nOwning SDET`s team backlog\nCommunicating with managers/PMs/POs/teams\nTasks prioritization\nPreparing for SAFe PIs\n\nSDET - Test Automation Functional Manager / HR Manager\nJune 2021\xa0-\xa0Present\xa0(1 year 7 months)\n\n- Hiring/Dismissal process (interviewing people from Belarus, Poland and\nIndia)\n- Building and managing a team of 7 people, different countries, different time\nzones\n- Career path development\n- Annual performance review for all team members\n- Moving the team from "Storming" to "Performing" state\n- Conflicts resolving\n- Trainings\n\n\xa0 Page 1 of 4\n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/pavel-stryhelski-462748bb?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3Bcv1tAQWtRwWiUc3HIErAyg%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/pavel-stryhelski-462748bb?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3Bcv1tAQWtRwWiUc3HIErAyg%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\n\n- Cross-team work on managing existing automation, moving automation\ntesting to Cloud, participation in testing strategy creation for an internal product\n- Working on identifying criteria for a new version (2.0) of existing automation\nframework\n- Interface between QA and Automation team\n\nTango Me\nLead Automation Engineer\nJanuary 2021\xa0-\xa0June 2021\xa0(6 months)\n\nBack-end application testing.\nTests as a Service (TaaS) for mobile applications.\nInterviewing people.\n\nTools:\nJava\\Kotlin + JUnit\nSpring Rest Template\nCucumber\nJenkins\nGoogle cloud/ k8s\n\nIDT Corporation\n4 years 11 months\n\nLead QA Automation Engineer, Guild Automation Lead\nFebruary 2019\xa0-\xa0January 2021\xa0(2 years)\n\n2019-2020 Financial Year Achievements:\n----------------------------------------------\n1) 1829 test cases have been automated ( worked with 1 my team and led\nautomation for four 3rd party teams located all over the world)\n2) 120 technical tasks have been resolved.\n3) 1372 flaky/bug tests have been fixed.\n4) Automation % for two big projects (9 minor included) has been increased\n8.8% --> 66.2%  ; 28.6% --> 70%\n5) 4 internal team members (my team) have been promoted to a higher level.\n6) At least 3 checks have been implemented to avoid accidentally broken build\n(BDD skipped steps, TestRail failed run creation, and etc)\n7) We have reviewed TestRail cases statistics (by written automated scripts)\nand created a graph that shows us the most frequently used cases. That has\nhelped to set priorities to cases and remove cases that are not currently used.\nThis helps to automate cases with maximum coverage and efficiency.\n\n\xa0 Page 2 of 4\n\n8) Pass rate for jobs maintained by us have at least 95,6%+ (300-500+ UI tests\nincluded in every job, 10+ jobs).\n9) Have conducted 2 trainings for Manual QAs (Java, RestAPI)\n10) Have written API base core lib (Java. TestNG, parallelization). It is used by\n2 members from courses (point 9) and they have written ~200 test cases using\nthis lib.\n11) Have helped DEVs to implement SONARQUBE analyzing (server) both for\nLinux and Win envs, .Net/dotnetcore/JS , written jenkins functions to use them\nin their pipelines, helped to implement and maintain this in their projects.\n12) I and a member from my team have created a possibility to perform Load\ntesting from AWS slaves using JMeter (jenkins function that can be used all\naccross the IDT teams) - maintain it and help teams to use it. \netc etc etc....\n\nQA Automation Engineer, Guild Automation Lead\nJanuary 2019\xa0-\xa0February 2019\xa0(2 months)\nBelarus\n\n- As an Automation Engineer:\neverything related to current automation processes.\nin charge of the progress of 3 team members\ncode review\nclosely work with testers (Managers, QAs) and devs to find better and right\napproaches for testing\n\n- As a Guild Automation Lead:\nin charge of code better practices/style, help other team members to solve\nongoing questions, provide solutions to refactor the existing framework to\nmake it more flexible/readable. Work with 3rd-party teams on implementing\ntests in the current framework. Leading IDT automation meetups.\n\n- As a build engineer / devops:\nend-to-end CI automation processes ( build-> store dlls -> run automation ->\nTR integration -> providing reports)\nJenkins, pipelines, groovy scripting\nand etc...\n\nSenior Automation Engineer (contractor at BelitSoft)\nMarch 2016\xa0-\xa0January 2019\xa0(2 years 11 months)\n\nQulix Systems\nTest Automation Engineer\n\n\xa0 Page 3 of 4\n\nNovember 2014\xa0-\xa0May 2016\xa0(1 year 7 months)\n\nAllied Testing\nQA Engineer\n2013\xa0-\xa02014\xa0(1 year)\n\nEducation\nBelarusian State University\nEnvironmental Chemistry\xa0·\xa0(2005\xa0-\xa02010)\n\n\xa0 Page 4 of 4'}}]}
