om\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/nuraym-askat-kyzy-7358a211b?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3BJdSkc%2FeRQUyQYAYIAObimQ%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/nuraym-askat-kyzy-7358a211b?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3BJdSkc%2FeRQUyQYAYIAObimQ%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\n\nEnvironment: macOS\nTechnologies: Slack,Browser Stack,Everflow software,WebPageTest, JMeter,\nMonosnap,Selenium, Python\n\nDats.team\nQA Automation Engineer\nмая 2021\xa0-\xa0декабря 2021\xa0(8 месяцев)\nRussia\n\nResponsibilities:\n-100% automation;\n-collaborate with the development team to analyze the application at the\nbackend level and to describe the defects;\n-testing mobile (iOS, Android), and web applications using various testing\ntools;\n-work with REST API;\n-work with bug tracking and test case management in JIRA, TestRail;\n-participating in daily Scrum meetings and sprint planning;\n-work with Confluence, Figma;\n-work with foreign partners;\n-writing autotests for mobile devices;\n-tested transactions with credit cards, debit cards, gift cards, coupons and\ncash;\n-performing load testing;\n-actively work with the command line;\n\nEnvironment: macOS, Linux.\nTechnologies: XCTest, Xcode, Swift, GitLab, Jira, TestRail, Confluence,\nAirtest, Charles testing tool, Python, Slack, Browser Stack, Atlassian (Jira,\nConfluence)\n\nAchievements:\n-implemented automation on iOS from zero.\n\nCodify Labs\nQA mentor\nфевраля 2021\xa0-\xa0июня 2021\xa0(5 месяцев)\nKyrgyzstan\n\nResponsibilities:\n-writing a curriculum from start to finish;\n\n\xa0 Page 2 of 5\n\n-teaching the basics of testing;\n-familiarizing students with testing tools;\n\nSpalmalo\nLead QA Engineer\nноября 2019\xa0-\xa0мая 2021\xa0(1 год 7 месяцев)\nKyrgyzstan\n\nResponsibilities:\n-50/50 manual and automation;\n-utilize a full range of testing methods, including functional, regression,\nintegration, installation, User Acceptance Testing;\n-create test cases and test procedures from prototypes, technical\nspecifications, requirements documents, and use cases;\n-create test plans, problem reports, status reports, and final test summary\nreports;\n-reviewed and approved test cases created by other testers. Worked closely\nwith the software development team in the resolution of problems;\n-conduct GUI and Black Box Testing using QTP and interacted with developers\nto resolve issues;\n-create automated tests using Selenium WebDriver for Continuous regression\ntesting (Jenkins &Ui Deploy) and reducing manual testing using Selenium,\nTestNG, and Maven;\n-created and executed test cases for the mobile version of the application.\nPerformed cross-platform compatibility testing;\n-tested, validated, and traced all types of transactions with cash, debit cards,\ncredit cards, and cheques for personal and business accounts, verified ATM\nlogs;\n-work with REST API;\n-tested mobile version of the application for Android and IOS;\n-used JIRA as a project tracking tool/Defect tracking/Test case Management\ntool;\n-work in Agile Environment with 2 weeks of Release cycle;\n-use in work Atlassian, Figma;\n-actively work with the command line;\n-testing software for various devices;\n-writing autotests for mobile and web applications;\n\nEnvironment: macOS, Linux;\n\n\xa0 Page 3 of 5\n\nTechnologies: Cucumber, Selenium, Appium, CI Jenkins, Ruby, Python,\nXcode, TestNG, Maven, Postman, Atlassian (Jira, Confluence), Selenium,\nGoogle sheets, MySQL\n\nO! Mobile Operator\nQuality Assurance Tester\nянваря 2018\xa0-\xa0ноября 2019\xa0(1 год 11 месяцев)\nKyrgyzstan\n\nResponsibilities:\n-develop manual test cases to test the functionality of the web and mobile\napplications;\n-knowledge of System Development Life Cycle (SDLC) of Waterfall and Agile\nMethodology;\n-prepared Defect Report as per severity and Priority;\n-performed the browser Compatibility testing for employee stock portal (IE9,\nFirefox, Safari, Google Chrome);\n-contributed to the test documentation: Requirements Traceability, Test Plan,\nTest Data Coverage Matrices, and Exit Reports;\n-created and executed manual test cases for transactions and GUI using HP\nQuality Center, verified test results in the database with SQL statements;\n-interact with developers to follow up on defects and issues;\n-testing backend and frontend parts;\n-work with REST API;\n-50/50 manual and automation;\n-experience with bug tracking and test case management in Atlassian\nproducts;\n-active use of the CRM system;\n-work with foreign partners;\n-testing software for various devices;\n\nEnvironment: Windows, Linux.\nTechnologies: HTML, CSS, Waterfall, Atlassian (Jira, Confluence), Selenium,\nJava, Python, Json, XML, Postman, Wireshark, PostgreSQL\nAchievements:\n-was able to complete the work of one service (which they had not been\nable to launch for two years before my arrival) and bring it to completion,\ncooperated with foreign partners;\n-once figured out the software code for the modem and managed to\nsuccessfully release these modems into operation;\n-took part in testing hundreds of the largest projects;\n\n\xa0 Page 4 of 5\n\n-in recent months I have been mastering test automation and writing small\ncodes (Python / Pytest);\n\n\xa0 Page 5 of 5', 'fields': {'name': None, 'birthdate': None, 'phones': None, 'email': 'askatkyzynuraym@gmail.com', 'salary': None, 'position': None, 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': [{'position': 'QA Automation Engineer', 'company': None}]}, 'parsing_meta': {'last_names_ignored': False, 'emails_ignored': False, 'phones_ignored': False}}
