ty with unit, mock, integration and functional tests.\n- Create new, update and configure exists application environments based on Linux using AWS.\n- Recurrent On-call activities.\n- Fixing bugs.\n\nGleb Kozlov - page 1\n\n<epam>\n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/gleb-kozlov-10a865138\n\n- Production monitoring, Issues investigation, troubleshooting.\n- Business correspondence.\n- Participation in project meetings with customer.\n\nTest Automation Engineer\nEPAM Systems\nOct 2016 - Oct 2017 (1 year 1 month)\nMain duty – test automation for application designed for US judiciary.\nThere we have a big test automation framework, which use Java+Maven+JUnit+Cucumber tools chain.\nFramework include tests as for UI, as for API.\nResponsibilities:\n- Performing UI automation testing of the core portal (and its implementations)\n- Maintaining and developing new features for the internal Java-based Test Automation Framework-\nMentoring junior automation testers\n- Contributing improvements into Test Automation Framework\n- Taking testing responsibility for the implementation: copying and tuning test scenarios from core\ntoimplementation, all testing release activities, communication with stream members (developers, BA,\nPM, manual testers, automation testers)\n- Executing regression testing, analyzing its results\n- Fixing automation bugs\n- Submitting and verifying production bugs\n- Issues investigation, troubleshooting\n- Business correspondence\n- Participation in QA and project meetings with customer\n\nJunior Software Test Automation Engeneer\nEPAM Systems\nSep 2016 - Oct 2016 (2 months)\n\nEducation\nMinsk Innovation University\nBachelor of Commerce - BCom, E-Commerce/Electronic Commerce\n2010 - 2014\n\nSkills\nREST APIs \xa0 • \xa0 Test Automation \xa0 • \xa0 Scrum \xa0 • \xa0 Jira \xa0 • \xa0 Design Patterns \xa0 • \xa0 Testing \xa0 • \xa0 Automation Testing \xa0 • \xa0\nAgile Methodologies \xa0 • \xa0 Software Development \xa0 • \xa0 SQL\n\nGleb Kozlov - page 2\n\n<epa