une 2021\xa0-\xa0Present\xa0(2 years 3 months)\n\n1. Manual (functional, API) testing and creation of the doc with evidences\n(screenshot for each acceptance) which should be attached to the main ticket\nof the User story.\n\n\xa0 Page 1 of 2\n\nmailto:kravchuk.ulia90@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/yuliya-krauchuk-027b28233?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3BXLVFpk91TXOx4lJp36aCYg%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/yuliya-krauchuk-027b28233?jobid=1234&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume%3BXLVFpk91TXOx4lJp36aCYg%3D%3D&licu=urn%3Ali%3Acontrol%3Ad_jobs_easyapply_pdfgenresume-v02_profile\n\n2. Creation automation test plans and test scenarios, assistance for\nAutomation QA.\n3. Participating in x-validation process: creation of test documentation (test\nplan, test cases, check lists), testing, bug creation and tracking bug fix\nprocess.\n4. Participating in Incident Management process: reviewing, investigating and\nreproducing bugs, as well as helping developers with dive into the essence.\n5. Requirements analysis and creation acceptance criteria for User Stories.\n6. Creation of test documentation (check lists, test-cases, test outlines) in Jira\nand TestRail and keeping them in updated state.\n7. Writing SQL queries for testing purposes.\n9. Leading and participating in meetings, creation reports with meeting-results.\n10. Being contact person for the customers and PMs, helping with business\nlogic.\n\nSavushkin Product plc.\nQA/QC Engineer\nAugust 2013\xa0-\xa0June 2021\xa0(7 years 11 months)\n\nEducation\nTechArt QA Students Lab - 2022\nJS Automation QA\xa0\xa0·\xa0(September 2022\xa0-\xa0February 2023)\n\nIT_Academy\nQA Manual\xa0\xa0·\xa0(February 2021\xa0-\xa0May 2021)\n\nThe Academy of Public Administration\nBachelor,\xa0Public Administration and Economics\xa0·\xa0(September 2015\xa0-\xa0June\n2018)\n\nBelarusian State Technological Univer