[2026-01-27 17:31:39,915: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104983783, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/d/7/7/d7782c5b8abb54ee5fff24811cf197f4.pdf/AQA%2520-%2520Panteleeva%252C%2520Valeria.pdf?s=B7dfx50PX2UhKooIY215GA&e=1769567499', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'AQA%20-%20Panteleeva%2C%20Valeria.pdf', 'text': 'Valeria Panteleeva \n\nTECHNICAL EXPERTISE \n\nQA EXPERTISE \n\nAQA EXPERTISE \n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE \n\nProject: Top 7 (June 2020 – Current) \n\nProgramming Languages \nand Frameworks Java, SQL, HTML, CSS, JSON, WSDL, XML, TestNG \n\nOperating Systems Windows, Android, iOS, MacOS\n\nDatabases MySQL Server, MongoDB\n\nTools and Technologies Browser Developer Tool, xPath, CSS, REST, SOAP, Postman, \nChrashlytics, Fiddler, Charles, SoapUI, Android Studio, xCode, \nIntellij IDEA, Salesforce, Jenkins, Bitbucket, GitHub, ReportPortal, \nBrowserStack, LambdaTesting, Selenoid, Selenium, Selenium Grid, \nDocker, TestNG, jUnit\n\nOther Confluence, MS Project, Jira, Trello, Google Docs\n\nRequirements Wrote team guidelines and project documentation, analyzed and \nvalidated projected requirements, use cases development, \nrequirements elicitation, requirements gathering, prioritization of \nrequirements\n\nTest Documentation Test documentation development: Test Plans, Test Scenarios, Test \nCases, Bug Reports. Analyzing Test Results, prepared Test result and \nQuality reports and sent to all stakeholders\n\nTesting Functional and Regression testing, UI testing, Smoke testing, Cross-\nbrowser testing, Web-services testing, Mobile testing\n\nOther API and Backend Testing by executing API requests and SQL queries, \nconducted Sprint demos to the Client, used JIRA issue tracking tool to \ntrack design defects and monitor test progress, established QA \nprocesses which reduced amount of bugs in new features, proposed \noptions for improving the final product, a lot of improvements were \nimplemented in the final product, review Guidelines (iOS Human \nInterface Guidelines, Android Design Guidelines), Salesforce org \nsetup and upgrade activities \n\nTest Documentation Auto test documentation development: Test Cases, Analyzing Test \nResults, Test Plan\n\nTesting Run auto tests locally and remotely, analyze results of auto tests, code \nreview and refactoring \n\nCoherent Solutions – Minsk, Belarus\n\n Page  of  1 4\n\n Valeria Panteleeva Resume \n\nRelease Advocate (QA Engineer / AQA Engineer) \n\nCustomer is the world’s premier provider of cloud and on-premise quality management software. \nQMS solutions help to lower risk, increase efficiency, and keep consumers safe while allowing \nmanufacturers, suppliers, and distributors to collaborate in a seamless and integrated environment. \nCompanies in life sciences and medical devices, consumer products, discrete manufacturing, and \nmore rely on Sparta. \n\n• Performed Release (include major, maintenance, and patches), Smoke, Functional and \nRegression manual testing \n\n• SFDC Configuration (process builders, flows, triggers), Apex coding and testing \n• Demos flow elicitation and gathering \n• Setup, configure and upgrade orgs for testing and Demos using production configuration \n• Test documentation development  \n• Translated Demo scenarios into regression tests \n• Reviewed support cases  \n• Identified potential upgrade challenges to determine fix or workaround \n• Prioritized resolution of customer reported defects \n• Improve upgrade & usage experiences \n• Provided feedback on issues encountered \n• Reviewed learnings of each release to provide organization wide guidance \n• Task management in JIRA \n• Test Cases Automation activities \n• Wrote Auto test scripts and scenarios \n• Run auto tests on BrowserStack/LambdaTesting \n• Analyzed results of auto tests on ReportPortal \n\nTools, Environment, Languages and Technologies: Salesforce, Web testing, JIRA, Confluence, \nPostman, Intellij IDEA, TestNG, Pr