[2026-01-27 17:32:35,829: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104984056, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/5/6/1/561ac59f80713227262652cbab6fc184.pdf/Pazniak%2520AQA%2520%281%29%2520%282%29.pdf?s=zrJB3EuLaHSp20LK8zCSAQ&e=1769567555', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'Pazniak%20AQA%20(1)%20(2).pdf', 'text': 'Yu l i y a  P a z n i a k  \nA u t o m a t i o n  Q A e n g i n e e r  \n\n+375 (29) 8226009 uliavetran@gmail.com \nLocation: Belarus  https://www.linkedin.com/in/yuliya-pazniak-5b4b50244/   \n\nI’m an automation QA engineer who has increased regression pass rate from 76% to 96% during 1 month in a new team. On \nnext project I according to customer’s desire investigate 3 different automation tool combination to choose the most \nsuitable option. I improve not only my hard skills, but also soft skills. And I always remember that product quality is a team \nwork.  \nI built testing processes on current project from the ground up, created pipeline in Azure DevOps(parametrized it, added \nschedule and conditions, variables), learnt JMeter to implement performance tests. At current moment I execute functions \nof manual, automation and performance engineer. \n\nS k i l l s  \nC# • Java • Git • JMeter • Gerrit • BitBucket • AzureDevops • Jenkins • Docker • MySQL • Maven • TestNG • Oracle SQL • \nxUnit • NUnit • SpecFlow • Postman • Fiddler • Selenium • Playwright • JIRA • TestRail • Allure • Visual Studio • Intellij \nIDEA • Microsoft Power Automate \n\nE x p e r i e n c e  \nSeptember 2022 – now \nFull-stack QA engineer (automation, manual and performance QA engineer) at HQSoftware \n\nResponsibilities:  \n- Developed a robust framework for automation testing to enhance test efficiency. \n- Created AzureDevops pipeline for executing automated test scripts. \n- Wrote comprehensive test cases to validate the proper functionality of web applications, including UI and API testing. \n- Prepared detailed product documentation highlighting testing procedures and outcomes. \n- Actively participated in daily meetings to discuss project progress and collaborate with team members. \n- Maintained and troubleshooted automated tests, addressing any issues or bugs as necessary. \n- Designed and implemented performance tests to evaluate system response and scalability. \n- Used AI for editing the documentation. \n- Conducted regression and smoke tests to ensure the stability and reliability of software releases. \n\nApril 2021 — September 2022 \nAutomation QA engineer at CJSC "Itransition" \n\nResponsibilities:  \n- Developed comprehensive test cases to verify the correct functionality of web applications through UI and API tests. \n- Conducted code reviews for fellow team members to ensure code quality and adherence to best practices. \n- Actively participated in daily team meetings to discuss progress updates, address challenges, and share achievements. \n- Facilitated weekly task estimation sessions and demonstrated completed test cases during demos. \n- Consolidated and streamlined SpecFlow steps by removing redundant ones. \n- Provided instruction and guidance to automation QA trainees to enhance their skills and knowledge. \n\nMarch 2012 — December 2020 \n1st category specialist at JSC “Belagroprombank” \n\nResponsibilities:  \n- Managed SWIFT transactions and insurance processes. \n- Oversaw credit operations related to real estate, cars, and other assets. \n- Responded to inquiries from government agencies and provided necessary documentation. \n- Assisted in handling arrests on accounts and facilitated secure money transfers. \n- Managed debit card operations and conducted public speaking engagements. \n- Maintained information stands in the service hall for easy access to relevant information. \n- Issued certificates to the embassy as required. \n- Conducted inspections of specific work areas to ensure compliance and efficiency. \n- Maintained a detailed journal of the BSO (Business Support Officer) activities. \n- Assumed the role of department head, overseeing and supervising departmental operations. \n\nE d u c a t i o n  \n2008-2012 \nPolesskiy State University \nBachelor\'s degree, Business/Managerial Economics \nBanking, Finance and Lending \n\n2012-2015 \nAcademy of Public Administration of the Republic of Belarus \nBachelor\'s degree, Business Administration and Management, General \n\nA d d i t i o n a l  e d u c a t i o n  \nJuly 2022 - English grammar courses. \nNovember 2021 - MySQL courses. \nDecember 2021 - Business English courses (31 lessons). \nApril 2021 - I finished English courses for qa engineer. \nJanuary 2022 – June 2023 – English courses \n\nC o r e  c o m p e t e n c i e s  \n-English – B2 \n-Strong networking and communication skills \n-Proactive', 'fields': {'name': None, 'birthdate': None, 'phones': ['+375 (29) 8226009'], 'email': 'uliavetran@gmail.com', 'salary': None, 'position': None, 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': None}, 'parsing_meta': {'last_names_ignored': False, 'emails_ignored': False, 'phones_ignored': False}}
