[2026-01-27 17:34:04,571: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104984544, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/9/9/9/999daa357bcf468a9572999d5a9a6885.pdf/Kirill_Zavelev_AQA_Java_CV.pdf?s=Ptmxzxq38Qqalu8DqmsaGA&e=1769567644', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'Kirill_Zavelev_AQA_Java_CV.pdf', 'text': 'Kirill Zavelev – Automation QA Engineer\nI work as a Quality Assurance Engineer for more than 5 years. Have experience in Automation in Java\n(Selenium, RestAssured), understand principles of developing automation tests and running them. Can\nbuild communication processes inside the team with developers and QEs. Was responsible for\nmentoring newcomers and providing knowledge transfer to them. Was involved in workforce and\nhuman resources management services testing, testing of web-applications in FinTech area. Working\nprocesses were carried out with SCRUM. Using best practices and techniques, I provide a valuable\ntesting process. Having experience in customer defects verification and in preparation necessary\nsystem environment, in preparation the versions of the application to be released. As a part of the\nteam, I have experience in communication with customer (taking part in groomings, plannings,\ndemos etc.).\n\nMajor skills\nPlatforms Windows/Mac OS\n\nLanguages and\nTechnologies\n\nJava 8, Selenium Webdriver, Selenide, RestAssured, TestNG,\nMaven, Allure, Postman, Atlassian stack (Jira, Bitbucket,\nConfluence), GitLab, Notion, Jenkins, Git, HP ALM (Microfocus\nALM), SQL, HTTP\n\nDatabases PostgreSQL\n\nTeam work Agile (SCRUM)\n\nLanguages Russian (native), English (B2)\n\nProfessional experience\n\n“Svaps Systems”, May 2022 – May 2023\n\nProject Oper\n\nProject description Development of web-applications in FinTech area for\nborrowers, brokers and banks of Europe\n\nPosition Senior QA Engineer\n\nTechnologies GitLab, Notion, Django, Sentry, PigeonLoft\n\nResponsibilities ● Functional testing\n● Requirements analysis\n● Bug reporting\n● Taking place in project meetings as representative of QA\n\nteam\n● Estimations and planning of QA activities\n● Leading of releases preparation and taking role of\n\nrelease manager\n● Holding regression and customer’s issues investigation\n● Deploying of testing environments\n● Fixing of broken configuration and pushing them to envs\n● Discussion of the features/issues with the team\n● Supporting and providing KT to new QA team members\n● Taking place in Retro and suggest possible improvements\n\nof the processes\n\nJSC “Arcadia Inc.”, February 2022 – May 2022\n\nProject SDO.COV\n\nProject description Development of web-applications and data warehouses for\none of the biggest international CRO (Contract Research\nOrganization).\n\nPosition QA Engineer\n\nTechnologies Microsoft SQL Server, JIRA\n\nResponsibilities Functional testing.\n\n“Epam Systems”, September 2018 – February 2022\n\nProject UKG (Ultimate Kronos Group)\n\nProject description Provides workforce management and human capital solutions.\nDeveloping of ‘Workforce Dimensions’ – large integrated system\nwith a lot of modules, including forecasting, timekeeping etc.\n\nPosition QA/AQA Engineer\n\nTechnologies and tools HP ALM, Jira, Confluence, TestNG, Selenium WebDriver, Jenkins,\nJava 8, Kubernetes, WinSCP, Right Scale\n\nResponsibilities ● Developing and maintaining automation tests\n\n● Working with Jenkins to run automation tests\n\n● Analyze automation reports and find the root cause of tests\nfailures\n\n● Carrying out Functional/Regression testing\n\n● Bug reporting\n\n● Carrying out Web-Services testing\n\n● Creating/Maintaining manual test-Cases\n\n● Requirement analysis\n\n● Communicating with the customer\n\n● Demonstration sprint results\n\n● Planning/Estimating scope of work\n\n● Close-knit work with QAs\n\n● Working with developers to reproduce the issues\n\n● Verifying defects, including customer related\n\n● Holding regression on customer environment\n\n● Deploying and managing cloud systems for testing purposes\n\n● Reading BE system logs on remote server\n\n“Arcom Group”, January 2018 – September 2018\n\nProject Arcom Ticket Service (ATS)\n\nProject description Arcom Ticket Service (ATS) - professional software that serves to\nautomate cinemas, theaters, concert venues, stadiums, museums\nand other cultural and entertainment centers\n\nPosition Junior QA Engineer\n\nResponsibilities ● Analyze requirements, writing check-lists, creating test-cases,\nbug-reports\n\n● Develop simple automation tests\n\n● Creating automation-related result reports\n\nEducation\n2013-2017 Belarusian State University. Faculty of Management and Social Technologies. Specialist.', 'fields': {'name': {'first': 'Kirill', 'last': 'Zavelev', 'middle': None}, 'birthdate': None, 'phones': None, 'email': None, 'salary': None, 'position': None, 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': None}, 'parsing_meta': {'last_names_ignored': False, 'emails_ignored': False, 'phones_ignored': False}}
