g role of\n\nrelease manager\n● Holding regression and customer’s issues investigation\n● Deploying of testing environments\n● Fixing of broken configuration and pushing them to envs\n● Discussion of the features/issues with the team\n● Supporting and providing KT to new QA team members\n● Taking place in Retro and suggest possible improvements\n\nof the processes\n\nJSC “Arcadia Inc.”, February 2022 – May 2022\n\nProject SDO.COV\n\nProject description Development of web-applications and data warehouses for\none of the biggest international CRO (Contract Research\nOrganization).\n\nPosition QA Engineer\n\nTechnologies Microsoft SQL Server, JIRA\n\nResponsibilities Functional testing.\n\n“Epam Systems”, September 2018 – February 2022\n\nProject UKG (Ultimate Kronos Group)\n\nProject description Provides workforce management and human capital solutions.\nDeveloping of ‘Workforce Dimensions’ – large integrated system\nwith a lot of modules, including forecasting, timekeeping etc.\n\nPosition QA/AQA Engineer\n\nTechnologies and tools HP ALM, Jira, Confluence, TestNG, Selenium WebDriver, Jenkins,\nJava 8, Kubernetes, WinSCP, Right Scale\n\nResponsibilities ● Developing and maintaining automation tests\n\n● Working with Jenkins to run automation tests\n\n● Analyze automation reports and find the root cause of tests\nfailures\n\n● Carrying out Functional/Regression testing\n\n● Bug reporting\n\n● Carrying out Web-Services testing\n\n● Creating/Maintaining manual test-Cases\n\n● Requirement analysis\n\n● Communicating with the customer\n\n● Demonstration sprint results\n\n● Planning/Estimating scope of work\n\n● Close-knit work with QAs\n\n● Working with developers to reproduce the issues\n\n● Verifying defects, including customer related\n\n● Holding regression on customer environment\n\n● Deploying and managing cloud systems for testing purposes\n\n● Reading BE system logs on remote server\n\n“Arcom Group”, January 2018 – September 2018\n\nProject Arcom Ticket Service (ATS)\n\nProject description Arcom Ticket Service (ATS) - professional software that serves to\nautomate cinemas, theaters, concert venues, stadiums, museums\nand other cultural and entertainment centers\n\nPosition Junior QA Engineer\n\nResponsibilities ● Analyze requirements, writing check-lists, creating test-cases,\nbug-reports\n\n● Develop simple automation tests\n\n● Creating automation-related result reports\n\nEducation\n2013-2017 Belarusian State University. Faculty of Management and Social Technologies. Specialist.'}}], 'middle_name': 'Викторович', 'files': [104984544]}
