riting test documentation, project documentation, useful guides\n- Testing: smoke testing, API testing (Postman), integration testing, security testing, white box testing,\nblack box testing, etc.\n- Communication with the development team, setting up processes, prioritizing tasks\n\nРезюме обновлено 13 ноября 2023 в 15:41 \n\nGJ rabota.by\n\n- White box testing using frontend and backend code, compilation of bugs based on its analysis (for\nexample, errors in calculating formulas for pagenation)\n\nI was the only QA in the web development department and achieved:\n1. I tweak development processes to improve productivity\n2. wrote helpful guides and documentation\n3. a significant number of critical errors were found, as well as a large number of errors associated\nwith incorrect project logic\n4. made many proposals for the development of the project, which improved the process of\ncommunication between departments and increased productivity\n\nИюль 2019\xa0—\nОктябрь 2019\n4 месяца\n\nQA Academy (1AQA)\nМинск,\xa0qa-academy.by\nИнформационные технологии, системная интеграция, интернет\n\n• Разработка программного обеспечения\n\nQA Engineer\n- Principles and methodologies of software testing.\n- Automated testing using popular tools and frameworks such as Selenium, TestNG\n- Creation and execution of test plans, development of test cases and scenarios.\n- Testing web applications, mobile applications, and other platforms.\n- Working with test management systems like TestRail\n- Requirements and specification analysis for effective test planning and execution.\n- Development of testing strategies and approaches to regression testing.\n- Debugging and reporting of bugs using issue tracking systems such as Jira\n- Fundamentals of security and performance testing.\n- Collaborating and communicating with developers, analysts, and other project stakeholders.\n- Best practices and current trends in QA and software testing.\nFundamentals of software testing, including its goals, processes, and methods.\n- Understanding of the software development life cycle and the role of QA within it.\n- Creation and execution of basic test scenarios and cases.\n- Utilizing manual testing to detect errors and issues in applications.\n- Writing bug reports and managing them.\n- Knowledge with principles of UI and functionality testing.\n- Knowledge of working with test management and issue tracking systems.\n- Communication skills for collaborating with the development team and other project stakeholders.\n- Knowledge the role of testing in ensuring software quality.\n\nОбразование\n\nВысшее\n\n2023 Белорусский государственный университет информатики и\nрадиоэлектроники, Минск\nФакультет компьютерных систем и сетей, Инженер-Программист (заочное обучение)\n\nТесты, экзамены\n2019 QA Academy\n\nQA Academy, QA Engineer\n\nЭлектронные сертификаты\n2019 QA-Academy\n\nStrelkov Sergey  •  Резюме обновлено 13 ноября 2023 в 15:41 \n\nКлючевые навыки\nЗнание языков Русский — Родной\n\nАнглийский — B2 — Средне-продвинутый\n\nНавыки  HTML      CSS      JIRA      MySQL      SQL      Agile      Scrum      Jenkins      Swagger \n\n Postman      REST      Json      Graphql      Bug Tracking System      Quality Assurance \n\n Test Methodologies      SQLite      Java Core      jQuery      PostgreSQL      Java      Git \n\n MongoDB      Kibana      Grafana      Selenium      TestNG      Maven      Allure      API \n\nДополнительная информация\nРекомендации Tipper Digital Systems\n\nAlexander Tarasov (Chief technical officer (CTO))\n\nОбо мне Experienced QA engineer witp knowledge of Java, test automation using Selenium and TestNG\nframework. Effectively performed functional, regression and automated testing in projects of\nvarious sizes.\n\nKnowledge of Java and experience with Selenium WebDriver allowed me to develop stable and\nefficient automated tests. I created test scripts, wrote test cases, and set up and maintained test\nenvironments.\n\nI have the skills to interact with developers, managers and other project participants, ensuring\nopen communication and high quality of the product.\n\nI always strive for self-improvement and learning new technologies in the field of QA in order to\nprovide modern and effective testing methods.\n\nOrganized and detailed, I am able to effectively manage time and resources to achieve my goals\nand meet deadlines.\n\nKnowledge of programming languages \u200b\u200bhelps me localize problems, understand where they may\narise from and what requires more detailed checks. I am constantly developing my skills and am\ncurrently learning Python\n\nStrelkov Sergey  •  Резюме обновлено 13 ноября 2023 в 15:41 \n\nИстория общения с кандидатом\nОтклики QA Engineer Automation\n\n9 ноября 2023\n\nAutomation QA Engineer (Mobile)\n6 декабря 2022\n\nПолучил отказ QA Engineer (Fullstack | Automation)\n20 июня 2023\n\nAutomation QA Engineer (Web)\n26 января 2023\n\nAutomation QA Engineer\n3 января 2023\n\nAutomation QA Engineer (Mobile)\n11 октября 2022\n\nStrelkov Sergey  •  Резюме обновлено 13 ноября 2023 в 15:41', 'fields': {'name': {'first': 'Sergey', 'last': 'Strelkov', 'middle': 'Aleksandrovich'}, 'birthdate': {'year': 2002, 'month': 2, 'day': 14, 'precision': 'day'}, 'phones': ['+375 (29) 8711394'], 'email': 'xakasp@yandex.by', 'salary': None, 'position': 'QA Engineer', 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': [{'position': 'QA Engineer', 'company': 'Tipper Digital Systems'}, {'position': 'Quality Assurance Engineer', 'company': 'TechStudio'}, {'position': 'QA Engineer', 'company': 'QA Academy (1AQA)'}]}, 'parsing_meta': {'last_names_ignored': False, 'emails_ignored': False, 'phones_ignored': False}}
