[2026-01-27 17:34:31,433: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-1] 🔍 Начинаем создание кандидата из данных: {'id': 104984673, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/a/7/a/a7a447785325967e1dc34a33ad311abc.pdf/Vitali_Nikalayenka%2520With%2520Photo%281%29.pdf?s=S3aq-YrgblL0b3UplQAJOQ&e=1769567670', 'content_type': 'application/pdf', 'name': 'Vitali_Nikalayenka%20With%20Photo(1).pdf', 'photo': {'id': 104984676, 'url': 'https://store.huntflow.ru/uploads3/named/0/c/c/0cc30398ad33d4e0a82f7d9eeacbe8f5.jpg/image0.jpg?s=3ARtfovqMoP532AB_I2wXA&e=1769567671', 'content_type': 'image/png', 'name': 'image0.jpg'}, 'text': 'nva87k@gmail.com \n\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/vitali-nikolaenko-127600179/ \n\n+375292309274 \n\nSkype: egik-kun \n\nTelegram: https://t.me/Egikkun \n\nVitali Nikalayenka \n\nOBJECTIVE I have around seven years of experience in QA. I have experience in testing web and mobile \napplications, including front-end and API. I have experience in test automation using C# + \nSelenium, TypeScript + WebdriverIO. \n\nPROJECTS April 2023 – nowadays Senior Software Testing Engineer \n\nProject: web application for traveling and migration for Relotech Solution.  \n\nTasks performed: planning testing on project, trainee training,  test cases creation, manual \ntesting,  API testing: create tests in Postman, take part in Scrum activities, creation of \nautomation tests for web application UI with WebdriverIO + TypeScript \n\nFEB-2022- April 2023 Senior Software Testing Engineer \n\nProject: Merge and tower defense game. Protect your cities against evil robots.  \n\nMerge Tower Bots - Apps on Google Play \n\nTasks performed: planning testing on project, test cases creation, manual testing,  API testing: \nautomate this process with Postman, integration testing, mobile testing, take part in Scrum \nactivities, checking application performance. I created new test flow for the game. I stated to \nuse performance testing with Apptim. We found several problems with performance as result.  \n\nJAN-2022-FEB -2022 SENIOR SOFTWARE TESTING ENGINEER \n\nProject Different words games: Free online puzzle games. Player tries to find hidden words. \n\nWord Pizza - Word Games - Apps on Google Play  \n\nTasks performed: planning testing on project, test cases creation, test cases review, manual \ntesting,  take part in Scrum activities, checking application performance, tracking test metrics, \nmentoring. I have found a lot of problems in development process of the project. I was the first \nperson who stated to create bugs during testing. I have suggested using of task estimation and \nusing branches in GIT and using merge requests. \n\nMAR-2020 -DEC 2021 SOFTWARE TESTING ENGINEER \n\nProject No Way To Die: Free online\\offline post-apocalyptic third person survival game.  \n\nNo Way To Die: Survival - Apps on Google Play \n\nTasks performed: planning testing on project, test cases creation, test cases review, manual \ntesting,  take part in Scrum activities, checking application performance, start planning \nautomation on project. Take part in discussion about gameplay and how to improve game. I \nhave created all test process from scratch for this project. I created an automation testing \nproject with “Unity Test Framework”. Auto tests covered part of smoke tests.  \n\nmailto:nva87k@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/vitali-nikolaenko-127600179/\nhttps://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.hypermania.merge.tower.bots&hl=us&gl=US\nhttps://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.openmygame.games.android.wordpizza\nhttps://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.openmygame.games.android.jsurvive&hl=us&gl=US\n\nPage | 2 Vitali Nikalayenka \n\nDEC-2019 - MAR-2020 - SENIOR SOFTWARE TESTING ENGINEER \n\nProject for finance company: development new functionality for desktop and web application.  \n\nTasks performed: test cases review, communication with other teams, take part in Scrum \nactivities, creation of auto tests in existing framework:  I u