dio Code, JetBrains Rider, Android Studio  \n\nCI/CD:  Jenkins, CircleCI, Azure, Blazemeter \n\nEducation \n\nBelarusian State University \n\nBachelor of Science in Physics \n\n Recent and major projects \n\nProject #1: \n\nItechart inner project \n\n05.2021-08.2021 \n\nStack: Microsoft Office, Atlassian JIRA, Chrome, Selenium, Java, PostgreSQL, Entity \n\nFramework \n\n Role: QA Automation Engineer \n\nProject \ndescription: \n\nIt is a tracking service of Itechart Group. The application allows take a vacation, \npaid/unpaid holidays and etc. This app contains information about every employee in \nthis company. \nApplication can switch between old and new version of API. \n\n Achievements: ○ Developed and maintained GUI test scripts to increase test coverage \n\n○ Analyzed test results to inform the team about the quality of the build \n\n○ Participation in daily meetings \n\nProject #2: \n\nNDA \n\n08.2021-11.2021 \n\nStack: Java, Selenium WebDriver, Rest-assured, Allure Framework, TestNG, Json and \n\nExcel Data Readers, GIT, Jira, BDD, Cucumber, Jenkins \n\n  Role: Senior Automation Engineer \n\nProject \ndescription: \n\nIt is a booking platform for taxis and limousines, which optimizes the booking process \nfor both, customers and drivers. With nowadays technology and its intelligent \nadoption to taxi and limousine booking customers and drivers can profit. This Win-\nWin is created by utilizing methods and technologies from the airline industry and can \nlead to a better route planning and capacity utilization of taxis and limousines. The \ndriver benefits through higher profits and revenues. The customer profits through \ndiscounts. \n\n  Achievements: ○ Maintained and improved existing automation framework to make it more stable \n\nand improve test performance. \n\n○ Fixed, created, executed automated test scripts for UI and API testing, \n\nmaintained ~60 automated tests. \n\n○ Participated in the process of knowledge transfer, checked the correctness of the \n\ncorrespondence of existing tests with the documentation. \n\nProject #3: \n\nJuicePlus+ \n\n11.2021-03.2022 \n\nStack: .NETCore/C#, BlazeMeter, Enity Framework Core, PostgreSQL, Selenium \n\nWebDriver, NUnit, Github, REST API, SyncFusion \n\n Role: QA Team Leader/Test Automation Engineer \n\nProject \ndescription: \n\nJuice+ is an online Multi-level Marketing platform that operated in the Health and \nWellness industry, specializing in providing customers with the concentrated best \nparts of 30 types of fruits, vegetables, and berries in capsule form. The company was \nin the process of upgrading their hardware and software system infrastructure and \nmoving to a new updated website and mobile platform. Our team's task was to audit \nthe current Juice+ systems, identify gaps and areas that need improvement and\\or \nupgrade and implement these upgrades along with the onsite team of Juice+ \nengineers. \n\n Achievements: ○ Participation in daily meetings \n\n○ Fixed, created, executed automated test scripts for UI and API tests. \n\n○ Сhecked the project performance in Blazemeter \n\nProject #4: \n\nSimpliGov \n\n03.2022-10.2022 \n\nStack: .NET Core, GitHub, NUnit, Allure, Selenium WebDriver, JMeter, TeamCity, Microsoft \n\nAzure, REST \n\n  Role: Senior Automation Engineer \n\nProject \ndescription: \n\nSimpligov is a system for automating daily routines related to the workflow lifecycle. \nThe system's functionality allows the creation of forms with different types of elements \n(text fields, text areas, password fields, address look-ups i.e.) and validation. Also, \nthere are signing the documents, merging the values from the fields into documents, \ncreating collaboration stages, and various other options. \n\n Achievements: ○ Anaylized/refactored/developed the test automation framework with .NET Core \n\nusing NUnit testing framework in the JetBrains Rider as IDE for testing \n\nWeb/REST API ○ Implemented automation smoke and functional tests ○ \n\nImplemented automation testing of REST API via HttpClient library ○ Built the \n\nproject as a part of stage deployment pipeline using Microsoft Azure ○ Configured \n\nand generated html reports from NUnit test results using the Allure reporter ○ \n\nPrepared analytical documentation for the customer showing the status of \n\nprogress ○ Managed Git repositories ○ Participated in daily standup meetings, \n\nplanning meetings, internal reviews and retrospective meetings \n\nProject #5: \n\nNDA \n\n10.2022 - Present \n\nStack: C#, Selenium WebDriver, NUnit, Entity Framework, RestSharp, SpecFlow, Microsoft \n\nGraph api, Java, appium, TestNG, BrowserStack, Azure(tfs) and Report Portal \n\n  Role: Senior Automation Engineer \n\nProject \ndescription: \n\nThe preeminent software platform serving the unique business development and \nexecution needs of firms engaged in the private capital markets. The platform is \nwritten in C# using ASP.NET MVC/WebAPI on the backend side, and React.js and \nRedux on the frontend side. Application has various integrations with third-party \nservices and applications like MS Word, MS Excel, MS Outlook, Evernote and \nnumber of integrations will grow. It allows our clients to build dynamic and \nconfigurable UI for tracking data and data relationships. Data is highly dynamic and is \nconfigured by the client (number of fields, fields’ types, fields’ relationship with other \nfields and so on). The application also has a mobile version written using Cordova \nwrapper and React.js/Redux on the frontend side. \n\nHobbies \n\nDancing, Swimming, Singing, Drawing, Reading, Yoga, \nSkiing"}}]}
