 compatibility resting\n\nJune 2020\xa0—\nDecember 2020\n7 months\n\nPixelPlex\nQA Engineer\n1.'Banking project' -blockchain sphere .\xa0Web.\n\n- A project related to the exchange of bitcoin/ethereum and ether for fiat money. Using API project\nhas actual price for every coin. Project was made with different roles of users\n\nResume updated 13 December 2022 at 02:43\n\nGJ rabota.by\n\n2.'Health care' project -medicine sphere . Web.\n\n- Project gives opportunities to make connection between people and doctors.\n\n3.'Property' project -blockchain sphere. Web\n\n- Project where user can buy possessions by smart contracts. Project related to the addition of\nproperties and purchase.\n\n4.'Сargo transportation' project. Web, mobile.\n\n- Project related to cargo transportation  with different users roles.\nApplication helps to find transport for customer`s cargo.\n\n5.'Sport project' - football sphere. Web, mobile.\n\n- Application where user can do rates, participates in rewards and challenges, gets prize and other.\nApplication was released in App store for IOS and Play market for Android.\n\nMy responsibilities:\n\n✔Creating, finding, reporting, validation bugs\n✔Improvements creation\n✔Apply different types of testing : smoke, extended, regression, GUI, usability, functional,\ncompatibility, mobile, API, positive, negative, black-box, usability testing etc.\n✔Work with Web version of application on different browsers\n✔Work with IOS version of application on different devices\n✔Work with Web version of application on different browsers\n✔Work with Android version of application on different devices\n✔PWA IOS version of application on different devices\n✔Work with PWA Web version of application on different browsers\n\nJanuary 2020\xa0—\nApril 2020\n4 months\n\nIntellectsoft\nQA Engineer\nJan, 2022 -Apr, 2022\n\nMedia project - Startup. Pilot web and iOS mobile version (similar to Netflix)\n\nMy responsibilities:\n\n✔Creating, finding, reporting, validation bugs\n✔Improvements creation\n✔Creating test documentation (test cases and checklist)\n✔Apply different types of testing : smoke, extended, regression, GUI, usability, functional,\ncompatibility, mobile, API, positive, negative, black-box, usability testing etc.\n✔Worked with IOS version of application on different devices\n✔Worked with Web version of application on different browsers\n\nEducation\n\nHigher\n\n2021 Safe (Scaled Agile) course\n\n2020 English course\n\nShuneyko Dmitry  •  Resume updated 13 December 2022 at 02:43\n\n2019 Testing course\n\nKey skills\nLanguages Belarusian — Native\n\nEnglish — B1 — Intermediate\n\nSkills  Optimistic for New challenges \n\n • Power and authority to take risks and make decisions      Positive sense of humor \n\n Adaptive to changing environments      Atlassian Jira      SQL      Regression testing \n\n Check-list      Manual testing      Git      CSS      Bug Reporting      Postman \n\n Agile Project Management      Test case      Jira      Black box testing \n\nFurther information\n\nAbout me I work as QA Engineer for 3 years and have experience and understanding how to test mobile\nand web projects,\nparticipated in 7 different projects.\nI have experience how work in product \xa0and outsourcing companies and \xa0understand workflow\nprocess clearly.\n\nShuneyko Dmitry  •  Resume updated 13 December 2022 at 02:43\n\nHistory\nResponses QA engineer (нагрузочное тестирование)\n\n14 December 2022\n\nShuneyko Dmitry  •  Resume updated 13 December 2022 at 02:43", 'fields': {'name': {'first': 'Dmitry', 'last': 'Shuneyko', 'middle': None}, 'birthdate': {'year': 1992, 'month': 3, 'day': 10, 'precision': 'day'}, 'phones': ['+375 (29) 6739366'], 'email': 'mailforpractice2021@gmail.com', 'salary': None, 'position': 'Manual QA Engineer', 'skype': None, 'telegram': None, 'experience': [{'position': 'QA Engineer', 'company': 'Aras corp.'}, {'position': 'QA Engineer', 'company': 'PixelPlex'}, {'position': 'QA Engineer', 'company': 'Intellectso